   "source": [
    "###  Counterfactual Analysis\n",
    "We investigate the effects of key economic parameters on individual consumption, savings, labor effort, and human capital accumulation. Our **baseline model** is defined as follows:\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "extract_all (generic function with 1 method)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 7,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "t = 1:model_baseline.simT\n",
    "\n",
    "function extract_all(model)\n",
    "    return (\n",
    "        c = mean(model.sim_c, dims=1)[:],\n",
    "        a = mean(model.sim_a, dims=1)[:],\n",
    "        h = mean(model.sim_h, dims=1)[:],\n",
    "        k = mean(model.sim_k, dims=1)[:],\n",
    "        income = mean(model.sim_income, dims=1)[:],\n",
    "        wage = mean(model.sim_wage, dims=1)[:]\n",
    "    )\n",
    "end\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Counterfactual 1: **Tax Rate Variations**\n",
    "\n",
    "We vary the labor income tax rate to examine its impact on work incentives and savings behavior.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Baseline:** τ = 0.25\n",
    "- **Low Tax:** τ = 0.10\n",
    "- **High Tax:** τ = 0.30 \n",
    "\n",
    "> 💡 **Interpretation:**  \n",
    "> Lower taxes increase disposable income, which leads to higher consumption and more asset accumulation. Higher taxes reduce both, while increasing labor disincentives.\n"
   ]
